     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical justification for 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum daily dose. It puts the patient at real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and the risk doesn't depend on normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note if you want it.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily**, if the goal is analgesia.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than that, I'd suggest the following:\n- Talk with pharmacy or the attending.\n- Consider adding acetaminophen or another agent.\n- Consider a different analgesic strategy.\n\nIf you want to proceed with a dose above the limit, it should go through your hospital's override process, with pharmacist review and a documented clinical rationale. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
